5. Database and Model Guidelines
Active Record Best Practices:
php// Proper model structure
class User extends ActiveRecord
{
    const STATUS_ACTIVE = 1;
    const STATUS_INACTIVE = 0;
    
    public function rules()
    {
        return [
            [['username', 'email'], 'required'],
            ['email', 'email'],
            ['status', 'integer'],
        ];
    }
    
    public function relations()
    {
        return [
            'profile' => $this->hasOne(UserProfile::class, ['user_id' => 'id']),
            'roles' => $this->hasMany(UserRole::class, ['user_id' => 'id']),
        ];
    }
}
Query Optimization:

Use eager loading to prevent N+1 queries
Implement proper indexing strategies
Use Query Builder for complex queries
Cache frequently accessed data

6. API Development Patterns
RESTful Controllers:
phpclass UserController extends ActiveController
{
    public $modelClass = 'app\models\User';
    
    public function behaviors()
    {
        $behaviors = parent::behaviors();
        $behaviors['authenticator'] = [
            'class' => HttpBearerAuth::class,
        ];
        return $behaviors;
    }
    
    protected function verbs()
    {
        return [
            'index' => ['GET', 'HEAD'],
            'view' => ['GET', 'HEAD'],
            'create' => ['POST'],
            'update' => ['PUT', 'PATCH'],
            'delete' => ['DELETE'],
        ];
    }
}
Response Formatting:

Use consistent JSON response structure
Implement proper error response format
Include appropriate HTTP status codes
Add pagination for list endpoints

